-# Business Rules — PegaFila
 
-Domain document for **PegaFilaWeb** — repository **frontend, backend and totem API** (Laravel monolith). Derived from product requirements; implementation does not exist in this repository yet.
 
-## MVP Scope
-
-Queue management (**pega fila**): ticket issuance, priority-based ordering, deterministic calling, and display across multiple channels.
-
-Out of initial MVP: features beyond the ticket → queue → call → display cycle.
-
-## Architecture (context)
-
-**PegaFilaWeb** concentrates frontend, backend and totem API in the same Laravel repository.
-
-| Layer | Technology | Lives in |
-| ----- | ---------- | -------- |
-| **Web frontend** (admin, attendant, TV, configuration) | Livewire, Bulma | PegaFilaWeb |
-| **Backend** (domain, queues, billing, auth) | Laravel | PegaFilaWeb |
-| **Totem API** (BFF — issuance, queues, locale) | Laravel (dedicated API routes) | PegaFilaWeb |
-| **Totem client** (UI, ESC/POS printing) | Flutter | Separate repository |
-| Database | MariaDB | Infra |
-| Subscriptions and billing | Asaas | Backend integration |
-| Transactional email | Resend | Backend integration |
-| Observability | Webhooks → Discord server | Backend integration |
-| Languages | Multilingual support | Web + totem API responses |
-
-The Flutter app (separate repo) is **client-only**: consumes the API exposed by PegaFilaWeb on web, desktop and mobile, without duplicating queue rules.
-
-## Business Organization
-
-### Entity
-
-An **entity** represents a client company. Each entity has:
-
-- An **access subscription** (limits and status via Asaas).
-- **One owner** (invariant rule).
-- **N users** linked (limit defined by plan).
-- **N ticket queues** (limit defined by plan).
-
-Limits (`x users`, `x queues`) come from the active subscription plan. Operations that exceed limits must be rejected. The number of users with access to each queue **is not limited**.
-
-### User Roles
-
-Every user belongs to **exactly one entity** per session context (no "global" user operating queues).
-
-| Role | Scope | Rules |
-| ---- | ----- | ----- |
-| **Admin** | Entity | Explicit access to everything in the entity. First account created in the entity is admin. |
-| **Owner** | Entity | Same operational access as admin, **except**: cannot be removed; every entity has **necessarily one** owner; ownership transfer only between admins; **only the owner** manages payment and subscription (Asaas). |
-| **Employee** | Entity | **Limited and granular** access (queues, screens and actions per assigned permissions). |
-
-**Invariants:**
-
-- Every entity has exactly one owner.
-- Owner cannot be removed while being owner; transfer ownership before downgrading or deleting.
-- Only owner accesses billing, plan and payment data.
-
-## User Administration
-
-| Action | Who can | Rules |
-| ---- | --------- | ------ |
-| Edit account | Admin, owner (own entity) | Profile data and preferences; respect plan limits. |
-| Reset password | Admin, owner | Reset flow for **account** (login) and **user** (entity member), per security policy. |
-| Remove account | Admin, owner | Not applicable to owner while being owner. |
-| Remove user | Admin, owner | Cannot remove the owner; employees lose immediate access to the entity. |
-| Assign role | Admin, owner | Users are **separated by role**; employees receive granular permissions, not admin/owner role. |
-
-## Queue and Tickets
-
-### Ticket
-
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
-
-- Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
-- Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
-
-### Priority
-
-Priority is an **integer**: the **higher the value, the more prioritized**. Named levels are configurable presets per entity that map to values; ordering uses the number, not the label.
-
-| Level | Value (example) | Description |
-| ----- | --------------- | --------- |
-| **Normal** | `0` | Standard service. |
-| **Priority** | `10` | Preference over normal. |
-| **Priority 80+** | `20` | Expanded priority range (e.g., age ≥ 80 years). |
-
-### Ordering and Fairness
-
-1. **Within same priority:** the **oldest** ticket is called first.
-2. **Between priorities:** higher priority value is called first.
-3. **Normal wait limit:** a **normal** ticket cannot wait more than **3 consecutive** priority tickets without being eligible for calling (fairness guarantee).
-
-The **next candidate queue** is **deterministic**: same state input → same next ticket, no random draw.
-
-### Call Panel (attendant)
-
-Three explicit actions, all deterministic:
-
-| Button | Behavior |
-| ----- | ------------- |
-| **Next (most important)** | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). |
-| **Priority** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). |
-| **Normal** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. |
-
-After each call, the ticket leaves the waiting queue and enters the session/display call history.
-
-## Display and Issuance Channels
-
-| Channel | Implementation | Function |
-| ----- | ------------- | ------ |
-| **Totem** | Flutter (separate repo) + **PegaFilaWeb API** | Client: issuance, queue selection, ESC/POS. Rules and state in this repo's backend. |
-| **Display screen (TV)** | Web frontend (browser) | Shows latest calls and waiting queue — read-only. |
-| **Selection screen (attendant)** | Web frontend (Livewire) | Call panel and queue operation. |
-| **Virtual** | Web frontend / API | Issuance without physical presence at totem. |
-| **Printed copy** | Totem client (ESC/POS) | Physical ticket; payload/format defined by API. |
-
-The **totem API** (BFF within PegaFilaWeb) exposes stable contracts for the Flutter client across all platforms (web, desktop, mobile).
-
-## Subscription and Access
-
-- Subscription status (Asaas) controls whether the entity can operate queues and create users.
-- Owner is the only role with permission to change plan, payment method and view invoices.
-- **Financial data is separated from entity:** located in `billing_accounts`/`subscriptions` (see [`database-schema.md`](database-schema.md)). Loading an entity does **not** return financial data — only when explicitly requested.
-- Asaas webhooks update subscription state idempotently (implementation: see Asaas skill when available in repo).
-- Transactional emails (invitation, password reset, billing notices) via **Resend**.
-
-## Observability
-
-Relevant operational events (webhook failures, queue errors, plan limits) can be forwarded by **webhooks** to a dedicated **Discord** server — only alerts, does not replace application logs.
-
-## Multilingual
-
-Web interface and **totem API** responses must support multiple languages; business rules (priorities, queue labels) are configurable per entity with locale fallback.
-
-## Technical References (implementation)
-
-- **Asaas:** subscriptions, webhooks, sandbox-first — document in `ai/skills/asaas/` when adding integration.
-- **Livewire:** validation, authorization and public properties in attendant panel — see stack security policy when `ai/` is in branch.
\ No newline at end of file
+**Display code sequencing:**
+- Code format `A<digits>` with at least 3 digits, zero‑padded. After `A999` the sequence continues without padding (e.g., `A1000`).
+- The next code is calculated from the last *valid* code in the queue, ignoring malformed legacy codes.
+- Deleted tickets do not reclaim numbers.
